#: ../../../index.rst:63
msgid "pip vs pipx"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../index.rst:65
msgid ""
"pip installs both libraries and applications into whatever environment is "
"active, with no isolation. pipx installs only applications, each in its own "
"virtual environment, and exposes their commands on your ``PATH``. You get "
"clean uninstalls, zero dependency conflicts between tools, and no ``sudo pip "
"install`` — pipx runs with regular user permissions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../index.rst:72
msgid "Where apps come from"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../index.rst:74
msgid ""
"pipx pulls packages from `PyPI <https://pypi.org/>`_ by default, but accepts "
"any source pip supports: local directories, wheels, and git URLs. Any "
"package that declares `console script entry points <https://packaging.python."
"org/en/latest/specifications/entry-points/>`_ works with pipx. `Poetry "
"<https://python-poetry.org/docs/pyproject/#scripts>`_ and `Hatch <https://"
"hatch.pypa.io/latest/config/metadata/#cli>`_ users can add entry points the "
"same way."
msgstr ""

